      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Libertarians prioritize individual liberty, arguing that individuals should be free from excessive government interference, including taxation. They contend that taxation infringes upon personal autonomy and property rights, as seen in the concept of the \"non-aggression principle.\" In contrast, social democrats believe that collective responsibility necessitates a more active role for government in redistributing wealth and funding public goods, as exemplified by the idea of social contract theory. This framework emphasizes the moral obligation to contribute to the common good and protect the vulnerable, which justifies a more substantial tax burden on individuals.",
